.TH "krep" "8" "" "" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
krep - maintain Kreato Linux repositories and build images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]krep\f[R] \f[B]check\f[R]|\f[B]update\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]krep\f[R]
\f[B]clean\f[R]|\f[B]lint\f[R]|\f[B]fmt\f[R]|\f[B]convert\f[R]
[\f[I]options\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]krep\f[R] \f[B]rootfs\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]krep\f[R] \f[B]iso\f[R]
\f[B]\[en]rootfs=\f[R]\f[I]directory-or-archive\f[R]
\f[B]\[en]output=\f[R]\f[I]directory\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.PP
\f[B]krep\f[R] \f[B]generate\f[R]
\f[B]matrix\f[R]|\f[B]markdown\f[R]|\f[B]manpage\f[R]
[\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
krep contains the repository maintenance and image-building
implementation in its own commands, modules, and data directories.
Existing configuration and runfile formats are unchanged.
krep replaces the removed chkupd, run3tools, kreastrap, and kreaiso
standalone tools.
It does not replace kpkg.
.PP
Use \f[B]krep \[en]help\f[R], \f[B]krep TASK \[en]help\f[R], and
\f[B]krep generate GENERATOR \[en]help\f[R] for complete task-specific
options.
.SH TASKS
.TP
\f[B]check\f[R]
Check upstream package versions without changing repository versions or
checksums.
Accepts \f[B]\[en]package\f[R], \f[B]\[en]repo\f[R], and
\f[B]\[en]backend\f[R].
Quote package wildcards to prevent shell expansion.
Network access may be required.
.TP
\f[B]update\f[R]
Explicitly attempt to update package versions and checksums from
upstream.
Review repository changes before committing them.
Unlike update, check never requests automatic package updates.
.TP
\f[B]clean\f[R]
Delete outdated archives from the cache selected by \f[B]\[en]dir\f[R].
This is not repository cleanup.
The default cache is \f[V]/var/cache/kpkg/archives/arch/amd64\f[R].
Requires root privileges.
.TP
\f[B]lint\f[R]
Check run3 files selected by \f[B]\[en]path\f[R], without rewriting
them.
.TP
\f[B]fmt\f[R]
Format run3 files selected by \f[B]\[en]path\f[R].
Rewrites files by default.
\f[B]\[en]check\f[R] only reports whether formatting is needed.
.TP
\f[B]convert\f[R]
Convert runfiles with \f[B]\[en]fromVer=2 \[en]toVer=3
\[en]path=PATH\f[R].
Prints the result by default.
\f[B]\[en]write\f[R] writes a sibling run3 file; \f[B]\[en]inPlace\f[R]
replaces the source.
Review and back up source files before writing conversions.
.TP
\f[B]rootfs\f[R]
Build a root filesystem with the existing kreastrap configuration format
and kpkg internals.
Requires Linux and root privileges.
.TP
\f[B]iso\f[R]
Build a live ISO from a trusted rootfs directory or tar archive.
Requires Linux, root privileges, and preinstalled host build tools.
Uses no mounts, loop devices, host kernel assets, or host package
installs.
.TP
\f[B]generate matrix\f[R]
Generate a JSON build matrix.
Accepts \f[B]\[en]repo\f[R], \f[B]\[en]output\f[R],
\f[B]\[en]limit\f[R], and \f[B]\[en]splitIfLimit\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]generate markdown\f[R]
Generate package documentation.
Accepts \f[B]\[en]pkgPath\f[R], \f[B]\[en]output\f[R], and
\f[B]\[en]all\f[R] for a repository.
Create the output directory before generating all package pages.
.TP
\f[B]generate manpage\f[R]
Convert Markdown manpage input to website Markdown with front matter.
Requires \f[B]\[en]file\f[R] and \f[B]\[en]output\f[R].
This does not generate roff output.
.SH IMAGE OPTIONS
.SS rootfs
.TP
\f[B]\[en]buildType=TYPE\f[R]
Configuration name.
Default: builder.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]arch=ARCH\f[R]
Target architecture.
Default: amd64.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]useCacheIfPossible=BOOL\f[R]
Reuse cached packages where possible.
Default: true.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]noSandbox\f[R]
Disable the kpkg sandbox for source builds.
Default: false.
Use only when an external chroot or other suitable isolation boundary is
already in place.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]configPath=FILE\f[R]
Use an explicit rootfs INI configuration instead of the selected
resource directory\[cq]s \f[V]arch/ARCH/configs/TYPE.conf\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\[en]overlayPath=DIRECTORY\f[R]
Use an explicit rootfs overlay directory instead of the selected
resource directory\[cq]s \f[V]overlay/\f[R].
The configuration\[cq]s \f[V]useOverlay\f[R] setting still applies.
.SS iso
.TP
\f[B]\[en]rootfs=PATH\f[R]
Trusted rootfs directory or tar archive.
Required.
The source is copied into a private workspace without modifying the
input.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]output=DIRECTORY\f[R]
Output directory for the ISO.
Required; created if needed.
Must be outside a directory input rootfs.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]init=PATH\f[R]
Absolute init path inside the rootfs.
Default: /sbin/init.
The init and its runtime dependencies and service configuration must
already be present.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]kernelVersion=VERSION\f[R]
Select a module version inside the rootfs.
Automatic only when exactly one version exists under
\f[V]/usr/lib/modules\f[R] or \f[V]/lib/modules\f[R].
Ambiguous or conflicting module trees are rejected.
The selected tree must contain \f[V]modules.dep\f[R], including when
\f[B]\[en]initramfs\f[R] is supplied.
Its resolved path must end in \f[V]/lib/modules/VERSION\f[R] (including
\f[V]/usr/lib/modules/VERSION\f[R]), not an arbitrary symlink target
elsewhere.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]kernelImage=PATH\f[R]
Absolute path inside the rootfs, not a host path.
Asserts that this image matches the selected module version.
By default, searches \f[V]/boot/vmlinuz-VERSION\f[R] then
\f[V]/boot/Image-VERSION\f[R]; \f[V]/boot/vmlinuz\f[R] and
\f[V]/boot/Image\f[R] are fallbacks only when the rootfs has one module
version.
Symlinks resolve within the rootfs.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]initramfs=FILE\f[R]
Existing host initramfs file to copy instead of generating one with
dracut.
Bypasses dracut and its host udev/tool preflight requirements, but not
rootfs kernel/module checks.
Must match the selected kernel and support the live layout: ISO label
\f[V]ISOIMAGE\f[R], \f[V]LiveOS/squashfs.img\f[R] containing
\f[V]LiveOS/rootfs.img\f[R] (ext4), and handoff to the selected
final-root init.
Contents are not validated.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]workDir=DIRECTORY\f[R]
Existing parent for a private build workspace.
Default: system temporary directory.
Must be outside a directory input rootfs.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]imageSizeMiB=SIZE\f[R]
Size of the ext4 rootfs image in MiB, not the final ISO size.
Default: 0 (automatic estimate).
Explicit sizes must be positive.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]clearRootPassword\f[R]
Clear the staged root password.
Default: false.
Requires a valid root entry in \f[V]/etc/shadow\f[R]; does not enable
autologin.
The source rootfs is not changed.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]name=FILE.iso\f[R]
Override the generated ISO filename.
Must be a visible filename ending in \f[V].iso\f[R], not a path.
Default: \f[V]kreatolinux-DATE-VERSION-KERNEL.iso\f[R].
Optional \f[V]/etc/kreato-release\f[R] metadata supplies
\f[V][General] dateBuilt\f[R] and \f[V]klinuxVersion\f[R]; missing
values default to the current date and \f[V]live\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\[en]overwrite\f[R]
Allow atomic replacement of an existing output ISO.
Default: false.
Does not bypass another build\[cq]s output lock.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]grubConfig=FILE\f[R]
Use an explicit GRUB template instead of the selected resource
directory\[cq]s \f[V]grub.cfg\f[R].
The template must contain \f[V]\[at]INIT\[at]\f[R].
.SS Both image tasks
.TP
\f[B]\[en]dataDir=DIRECTORY\f[R]
Override the command-specific asset directory.
For rootfs this directory contains \f[V]arch/\f[R] and optionally
\f[V]overlay/\f[R].
For iso it contains \f[V]overlay/\f[R], \f[V]overlays/\f[R], and
\f[V]grub.cfg\f[R].
This takes precedence over normal resource lookup.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\f[B]KREP_DATA_DIR\f[R]
Unified image resource root containing \f[V]rootfs/\f[R] and
\f[V]iso/\f[R] children.
Unlike \f[B]\[en]dataDir\f[R], this selects the parent data root, not
one command\[cq]s directory.
When using sudo, ensure the variable is passed to the privileged
process.
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[V]krep/data/rootfs/\f[R], \f[V]krep/data/iso/\f[R]
Source image resources.
.TP
\f[V]out/krep\f[R], \f[V]out/share/krep/\f[R]
Build-tree executable and image resources, produced by \f[B]make
krep\f[R].
.TP
\f[V]PREFIX/bin/krep\f[R], \f[V]PREFIX/share/krep/\f[R]
Installed executable and image resources.
\f[B]make install_krep\f[R] defaults to \f[V]PREFIX=/usr/local\f[R].
\f[B]DESTDIR\f[R] stages a package without changing the runtime prefix.
For example, \f[B]make install_krep PREFIX=/usr
DESTDIR=/tmp/package\f[R].
.TP
\f[V]share/krep/rootfs/arch/ARCH/configs/TYPE.conf\f[R]
Existing kreastrap INI configuration, described in kreastrap.conf(5).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Check versions without updating packages:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
krep check --package=\[aq]*\[aq] --repo=/path/repo --backend=repology
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Explicitly update one package:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
krep update --package=example --repo=/path/repo --backend=repology
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Check formatting without writing:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
krep fmt --path=/path/repo --check
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Build images with explicit resources:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
sudo krep rootfs --arch=amd64 --dataDir=/opt/assets/rootfs
sudo krep iso --rootfs=/path/rootfs.tar.gz --output=/path/images --dataDir=/opt/assets/iso
\f[R]
.fi
.SH ISO HOST REQUIREMENTS
.PP
ISO executable preflight always requires \f[B]cp\f[R],
\f[B]truncate\f[R], \f[B]mkfs.ext4\f[R], \f[B]mksquashfs\f[R],
\f[B]grub-mkrescue\f[R], and \f[B]xorriso\f[R] on PATH.
Archive input also requires \f[B]tar\f[R] with GNU-compatible
extraction, ownership, extended-attribute (\f[V]--xattrs\f[R],
\f[V]--xattrs-include=*\f[R]), and ACL (\f[B]\[en]acls\f[R]) options.
Without \f[B]\[en]initramfs\f[R], preflight also requires
\f[B]dracut\f[R], \f[B]udevadm\f[R], \f[B]depmod\f[R],
\f[B]modprobe\f[R], \f[B]dmsetup\f[R], and \f[B]switch_root\f[R].
Install these tools before building; krep does not install them for ISO
assembly.
.PP
Executable preflight is not a complete dependency check.
Supply a compatible native-architecture toolchain, dracut shell/live
modules and dependencies, and a working host udev provider with daemon
and rules when generating an initramfs.
The dracut toolchain and GRUB platform must match the target
architecture.
Dracut site configuration is suppressed, but vendor and runtime drop-ins
can still apply; host configuration is not fully isolated.
No host kernel is required: the kernel and modules come from the rootfs.
GRUB needs platform modules for each target firmware mode, such as
\f[V]i386-pc\f[R] for x86 BIOS and \f[V]x86_64-efi\f[R] for x86-64 UEFI,
plus its platform packaging dependencies (such as mtools for EFI image
creation).
Secure Boot is not configured.
The target kernel must support the host-generated ext4 features,
required live/storage drivers, and target hardware firmware.
Architecture compatibility is not checked; arbitrary cross-builds are
not configured.
.SH WARNINGS
.PP
Both image tasks require Linux and root privileges.
Rootfs builds can install host packages and use chroots and mounts.
ISO assembly uses no mounts or loop devices; root is needed to preserve
ownership and device nodes.
Use trusted inputs and overlays only.
Arbitrary untrusted archive extraction as root is unsupported.
.PP
The rootfs must supply its own working init, runtime, and services.
Init path checks do not verify libraries or service configuration; the
builder cannot generate every init system\[cq]s configuration.
\f[V]/etc/kreato-release\f[R] is optional.
Its \f[V][Core] init\f[R] field selects only an optional init-specific
overlay.
Passwords are preserved by default.
Bundled resources do not configure autologin or remove firstboot
services; custom overlays may intentionally change this policy.
\f[B]\[en]clearRootPassword\f[R] produces an empty root password; do not
treat such an image as a secure installed system.
.PP
ISO builds use private \f[V]krep-iso-*\f[R] workspaces and adjacent
\f[V]NAME.iso.lock\f[R] directories.
Different output names can build concurrently.
A second build for a locked output fails.
Publication is atomic; unfinished output is not published as the final
ISO.
Normal completion, errors, SIGINT, and SIGTERM clean up owned
workspaces, partial files, and locks.
SIGKILL, power loss, or cleanup failures can leave stale workspaces,
output \f[V].krep-iso-*.partial\f[R] files, and locks.
Locks are not automatically reclaimed.
Verify that no build or child process uses these paths before removing
them manually.
.PP
Compilation and unit tests do not prove bootability.
Linux integration and VM boot validation remain required before release;
no boot-verified claim is made.
Inspect the initramfs and test each intended BIOS/UEFI mode, live-root
handoff, console login, and shutdown.
See \f[V]krep/ISO.md\f[R] for detailed requirements.
